    "description": "Raise the default reviewer effort from low to medium\n\nThe reviewers now run at medium effort by default. Before, they ran at low effort.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Each built-in reviewer in `prompts/reviewers/*.md` has `effort: medium` in its frontmatter. The frontmatter value is the effective default when no repo config sets the effort.\n- The `reviewer` role in `ROLE_DEFAULTS` (`src/config/models.ts`) has effort `medium`. The run record shows this value as the reviewer role's effort.\n- The README and `docs/design/high-level-design.md` show the new default. The first harness experiment in section 5.1 now compares Opus 5.5 at medium with Opus 5.5 at low and with Sonnet 5.5 at medium.\n- The tests that expected `low` now expect `medium`. One test in `test/repo-config.test.ts` sets `models.reviewer.effort`. That value changes from `medium` to `high`, so it differs from the new default and the test still shows that the repo config takes precedence over the frontmatter.\n\n## Release\n\nA consumer repo gets this change only when the SHA in `review.yml` moves. Follow \"The release tag\" in the README.\n\n## Checks\n\n`npm test` (1061 pass), `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck` and `npm run build` all pass.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01UKXoH72K6RLXNCGUFmHPfP\n",
